Description: Num Lock and Caps Lock as in i3 (bindings, IPC state, run time)
 Key bindings ignored Num Lock: bindsym KP_End fired whether Num Lock was on
 or off, bindsym Mod2+KP_1 never fired and bindcode 87 fired in both states.
 Bindings now follow Num Lock as in i3: a key matches keysym bindings through
 the keysym it yields in the current Num Lock state, Mod2 in a binding needs
 Num Lock on, and a keycode binding without Mod2 fires with Num Lock on only
 when Num Lock leaves the keysym of the key unchanged. Unlike i3, a plain
 bindsym KP_1 fires for the keypad 1 key while Num Lock is on.
 .
 get_inputs (and get_seats) report xkb_num_lock and xkb_caps_lock for each
 keyboard, the state of its group for a grouped keyboard, and an input event
 with the change xkb_locks is sent when they change (swaywm/sway#4889).
 .
 xkb_numlock and xkb_capslock are accepted at run time: the lock is turned
 on or off once, on the matching keyboards (on the group of a grouped one),
 and the focused client receives the new state. Virtual keyboards are left
 alone.
 .
 The three upstream commits, squashed. On top of 07-keyboard-accessibility,
 the lock fields follow its accessibility fields in get_inputs and the man
 page; mouse keys still take the keypad keys before bindings whatever the
 Num Lock state.
